<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vakil Bath</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil">Vakil</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a> is a historic public bathhouse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, built under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan</a> during the Zand period. It forms part of the architectural ensemble with which he adorned his capital. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> list it with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil-bazaar">Vakil Bazaar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil-mosque">Vakil Mosque</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arg-of-karim-khan">Arg of Karim Khan</a> as among the finest examples of eighteenth-century Persian architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vakil-bath.jpg" alt="Vakil Bath" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ba%C3%B1os_de_Vakil,_Shiraz,_Ir%C3%A1n,_2016-09-24,_DD_39-41_HDR.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
